 *
 * This API operation enables the registration of a new AI training dataset in
 * the ai_training_data table, as part of the AdvancedAI module. The
 * ai_training_data table is dedicated to cataloguing all datasets—internal or
 * external—utilized during AI/ML model training. This operation allows
 * administrators or automated pipelines to create a new dataset entry,
 * recording metadata such as name, version, source_uri, schema hash, record
 * count, and its association to a specific model (optional).
 *
 * Upon POST, the system will validate the uniqueness of the combination (name,
 * version, source_uri) to avoid redundant records. If associated with an AI
 * model, it checks referential integrity with the ai_models table. Required
 * fields must be present, and audit/evidence records will be generated for
 * traceability.
 *
 * Security is maintained through permission checks, and actions are logged
 * immutably for regulatory, audit, and explainability compliance. This endpoint
 * is typically consumed by model management pipelines and admin/operator UIs
 * before initiating training or model retraining workflows.
 *
 * Failure scenarios include duplication, missing required fields, or model
 * linkage errors, all of which return detailed error messages with evidentiary
 * context for compliance and debugging. Related API operations include PATCH
 * for listing/searching datasets, PUT for updates, and DELETE for
 * removal/revocation.
 *
 * @param props.connection
 * @param props.body Creation info for a new AI training dataset.
 * @path /advancedAI/aiTrainingData
 * @autobe Generated by AutoBE - https://github.com/wrtnlabs/autobe
